{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/persistencecoordinator\/mergechanges(into:policy:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"text":"MainActor","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mergeChanges","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"into","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"store","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"policy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MergePolicy","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"store","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The live store to reconcile.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"policy","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Narrows the configured policy for this call only.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is what a remote-change observer should call. Where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/rehydrate(into:policy:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" re-reads every row of every registered entity","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on every tick, this reads the store’s transaction log since the last","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"merge and spends the result through ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/mergeRemote(into:ids:deleted:policy:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"— so a tick on an N-row table where k rows changed costs O(k). A tick with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no transactions behind it costs one history fetch and nothing else.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every guarantee the other two make holds here. Deletions come from history","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tombstones, which are positive evidence, so unlike a full re-hydration this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"can"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" remove the last surviving row. Pending local writes and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceCoordinator\/editing","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds still win, and that is not configurable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"When it re-reads everything instead","anchor":"When-it-re-reads-everything-instead","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The narrow path is an optimisation, never a weakening: anything that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves a window unaccounted for falls back to the full read, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fallback keeps its empty-snapshot guard. It happens on the first tick","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after launch or a container rebuild, when the watermark has expired or the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"history fetch fails, when a deletion’s tombstone carries no identity","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(every row deleted before ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Attribute(.preserveValueOnDeletion)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shipped),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when a changed row can’t be resolved, and when more than one store sits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behind the container.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The watermark advances whenever a tick read every registered entity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successfully — including a tick that declined to apply some of what it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read. A row an editing hold defers is carried forward by identity and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-offered next tick, which is what keeps a hold from quietly becoming a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"veto without costing a full table read per tick to prevent. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:HowToAddICloudSync"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both outcomes are reported: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/Kind-swift.struct\/remoteChangesMerged","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a narrowed tick, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/Kind-swift.struct\/historyUnavailable","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a reason for a fallback. A narrowed tick counts what it re-offered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"separately from what it merged, so a hold that is never released — which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"makes every tick re-offer the same rows forever — reads as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/carriedOverCount","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" equal to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/mergedCount"},{"text":", rather than as healthy traffic.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mergeChanges"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"into"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux5StoreC","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Store"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"policy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiduxPersistence11MergePolicyV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MergePolicy"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}],"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence0B11CoordinatorCAA0A00A10ObservableRzrlE12mergeChanges4into6policyyAD5StoreCyxq_G_AA11MergePolicyVSgtYaF","title":"mergeChanges(into:policy:)","extendedModule":"SwiduxPersistence","roleHeading":"Instance Method","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"